<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S10.T7.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="S10.T7.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:113%;">DL3DV <math id="S10.T7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{V_{C}}\mathbf{{=}4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟒</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{V_{C}}\mathbf{{=}4}</annotation></semantics></math>, SVSM Encoder-Decoder.<span id="S10.T7.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> SVSM Encoder-Decoder model settings used to sweep scaling laws for the multi-view (<math id="S10.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{C}&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{C}&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>) novel view synthesis setting. </span>Bolded<span id="S10.T7.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> is the row for the compute-matched, Pareto-optimal SVSM model compared against the 24-layer LVSM Decoder-only model.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
